{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1946","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1946","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1946\",\"parent_revision\":\"b11559366d3c21d660ed5d313437397857c13b7a\",\"root_revision\":\"21bc078bdbadff2f79890d33d114640768f6b81cecba87e1fe82123f86f51c72\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll claims verified against primary source files on 2026-05-02.\\\\n\\\\n| Claim | Source | Verdict |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| redact.py does not exist | Read: scripts/redact.py \u2192 \\\\\\\"File does not exist\\\\\\\" | CONFIRMED |\\\\n| monitor.py:369 builds content field without filtering | Read: monitor.py lines 362-375 | CONFIRMED \u2014 `content = \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\".join(line.rstrip() for line in content_lines)` at line 369, passed to `_emit` at line 370 |\\\\n| spawn.py cmd_read prints raw pane stdout | Read: spawn.py lines 816-842 | CONFIRMED \u2014 `print(result.stdout, end=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")` at line 842 in `cmd_read`; cited line 749 is a `tmux new-session` call, NOT the pane read |\\\\n| health.py:226-227 prints capture_pane_by_id return | Read: health.py lines 224-227 | CONFIRMED |\\\\n| health.py:97-100 prints JSONL snippet and text snippet | Read: health.py lines 94-100 | CONFIRMED |\\\\n| abtop uses redact_secrets() with sk-ant-, sk-proj-, ghp_ patterns | Read: research/developer-tools/abtop.md line 194 | CONFIRMED \u2014 `src/collector/mod.rs pub(crate) fn redact_secrets()` |\\\\n| No existing redact function in kage-bunshin | Confirmed by redact.py non-existence and prior grep evidence | CONFIRMED |\\\\n\\\\n**Correction to prior grooming:** spawn.py emission point was cited as line 749. Actual emission line is 842 (`print(result.stdout, end=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")` in `cmd_read`). Line 749 is part of `cmd_spawn`, unrelated to pane reading.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add secret redaction to kage-bunshin monitor pane capture before emission** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/abtop.md \u2014 pattern: redact_secrets() filters sk-ant-, sk-proj-, ghp_, etc. before UI display\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\\\n\\\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Redact secrets from kage-bunshin pane captures before emission |\\\\n| Emission points | AVAILABLE | 4 emission points across 3 files verified against source (see Fact-Check) |\\\\n| Secret pattern definition | DERIVABLE | Target State section lists full pattern set: sk-ant-*, sk-proj-*, sk-*, ghp_*, gho_*, ghs_*, github_pat_*, AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}, Bearer [A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,} |\\\\n| Test harness approach | DERIVABLE | Derivable from pattern list and existing pytest infrastructure |\\\\n| Extensibility mechanism | MISSING | Whether patterns are env-var extensible or module-level only not yet decided \u2014 human input needed |\\\\n| Redaction display format | MISSING | [REDACTED] vs [REDACTED:TYPE] \u2014 human input needed |\\\\n\\\\n**Gaps affect:** test assertions (display format) and implementation surface (extensibility). Neither blocks writing the core redact module or wiring call sites \u2014 both can be deferred to implementation.\\\\n\\\\n**Effort: Small.** Four emission points across three files, one new redact.py stdlib module, one test file.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. In a kage-bunshin-monitored tmux session, run a command that prints a credential \u2014 e.g. `echo ghp_AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA`.\\\\n2. Run `uv run monitor.py poll --session-id <id>` against that session.\\\\n3. Observe the emitted JSON `content` field \u2014 it contains the raw token string.\\\\n4. Alternatively, run `uv run spawn.py --session-id <id> read --name <session>` and observe the printed pane output contains the raw token.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Secret leakage via monitor pane capture affects any kage-bunshin user. The attack surface is always active: every pane poll, every `read` command, every health check. The fix is small and fully bounded. P1 classification is appropriate.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen pane content is captured via tmux capture-pane and is about to be included in any emitted JSON or printed output, all strings matching the secret redaction patterns are replaced with [REDACTED] before emission. The substitution happens at a single choke-point (a redact() function) called before every emission point.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `monitor.py poll` on a session whose tmux pane contains a string matching any pattern in PATTERNS emits `intervention_needed` JSON with that string replaced by `[REDACTED]`.\\\\n2. Running `spawn.py read` on a session whose pane contains a secret pattern prints the pane content with that string replaced by `[REDACTED]`.\\\\n3. Running `health.py capture` on a pane containing a secret pattern prints `[REDACTED]` rather than the raw value.\\\\n4. `health.py` extract_actions output (inp and snippet strings) replaces secret-matching substrings with `[REDACTED]`.\\\\n5. The `redact()` function is the single call site for all four emission points \u2014 no emission point bypasses it.\\\\n6. Adding a new pattern to PATTERNS causes that pattern to be redacted across all four emission points without any other code changes.\\\\n7. Pane content containing no secret patterns passes through unchanged \u2014 no false positives on normal output.\\\\n8. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/redact.py` exits 0.\\\\n9. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/tests/test_redact.py` exits 0.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should the PATTERNS list be extensible at runtime via an environment variable (e.g. `KAGE_BUNSHIN_EXTRA_REDACT_PATTERNS=pattern1,pattern2`) or is the module-level list sufficient for current needs?\\\\n- Should redacted output show `[REDACTED]` (generic, more secure) or `[REDACTED:TYPE]` (e.g. `[REDACTED:GITHUB_TOKEN]`, aids debugging but leaks token type)?\\\\n\\\\nNote: Implementation can proceed with `[REDACTED]` and a module-level PATTERNS list as defaults if no answer is provided before work starts.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Skill | /dh:kage-bunshin |\\\\n| Prior art | research/developer-tools/abtop.md (line 194) \u2014 abtop redact_secrets() pattern reference |\\\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py (line 369 \u2014 content field) |\\\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py (line 842 \u2014 cmd_read print) |\\\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/health.py (lines 97-100, 226-227) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Extensibility mechanism is MISSING: whether PATTERNS is env-var extensible (e.g. KAGE_BUNSHIN_EXTRA_REDACT_PATTERNS) or module-level only has not been decided. Blocks finalizing the module interface but not the core implementation.\\\\n- Redaction display format is MISSING: `[REDACTED]` vs `[REDACTED:GITHUB_TOKEN]` \u2014 affects test assertions. Defaults to `[REDACTED]` if not specified.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 one new 30-40 line stdlib module (redact.py), one test file, four 1-line import+call changes across three existing files. The pattern list is specified in Target State. No external dependencies. No schema or API changes.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\\\n|------|--------|\\\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/redact.py (new) | New stdlib-only module: PATTERNS list of compiled regexes, `redact(text: str) -> str` function |\\\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py | Import redact; apply before `content =` assignment at line 369 |\\\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py | Import redact; apply to `result.stdout` before `print()` at line 842 |\\\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/health.py | Import redact; apply at lines 97-100 (inp/snippet) and 226-227 (capture content) |\\\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/tests/ (new test file) | Test redact() with matching and non-matching inputs |\\\\n\\\\n**No changes outside kage-bunshin/scripts/.** The redact module is local to the kage-bunshin skill, not a shared harness utility.\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nredact.py design: PATTERNS is a list of compiled regexes. redact(text: str) -> str applies each pattern, replacing matches with [REDACTED]. The function is pure (no side effects) and testable in isolation.\\n\\nPattern candidates (require human confirmation \u2014 this is the MISSING input):\\n- Environment variable values: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=..., GITHUB_TOKEN=..., AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...\\n- Bearer token format: Bearer [A-Za-z0-9+/=_-]{20,}\\n- Generic hex secrets: [0-9a-f]{40,} (git SHA length and above)\\n\\nThe pattern list must be configurable (not hardcoded constants) to allow teams to add project-specific patterns without modifying the module.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** Feature \u2014 new stdlib module (`redact.py`) plus wire-up at 4 existing emission points.\\\\n\\\\n**Security posture:** Defense-in-depth. The root cause is the absence of a redaction layer at the pane-capture boundary. This is not a data-flow bug in existing code \u2014 it is a missing capability.\\\\n\\\\n**Scope:** Contained to `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/`. No cross-plugin changes required.\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an orchestrator reading kage-bunshin pane captures, I want secrets (API keys, tokens, credentials) to be automatically redacted from captured output before it is emitted to orchestrator-facing JSON, so that sensitive values are never exposed in logs, intervention notifications, or any downstream consumer.\\n\\n### Verified Emission Points\\n\\nAll in plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/:\\n\\n1. **monitor.py:369** \u2014 intervention_needed JSON content field \u2014 joins last 10 pane lines without any filtering\\n2. **spawn.py:749** \u2014 cmd_read prints raw tmux capture-pane stdout directly\\n3. **health.py:226-227** \u2014 capture_pane_by_id() return value printed to terminal\\n4. **health.py:97-100** \u2014 extract_actions() \u2014 JSONL input snippet and text snippet both printed without filtering\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA `redact_secrets(text: str) -> str` function in a shared module (e.g. `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` companion or new `plugins/development-harness/redact.py`) masks: `sk-ant-*`, `sk-proj-*`, `sk-*`, `ghp_*`, `gho_*`, `ghs_*`, `github_pat_*`, AWS access key IDs (`AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}`), and bearer tokens of the form `Bearer [A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}`. `monitor.py._capture_pane` and `_emit` route all string fields through it. Same function reused by `kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py` log capture and any future TUI dashboard.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAdd a unit test at `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_redact.py` with cases asserting `redact_secrets(\\\"sk-ant-api03-abcdef...\\\")` returns `\\\"sk-ant-***\\\"` (or similar mask). Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_redact.py` \u2014 exit 0. Grep of `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py` shows `redact_secrets` imported and applied to `_capture_pane` output before emission.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py` prints session pane captures via `_capture_pane` (line 203) and emits payloads via `_emit` (line 145). There is no `redact_secrets`-equivalent function in `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/`. Grep of `plugins/development-harness/` for `redact`, `mask_token`, `sk-ant`, `ghp_` returns zero matches. tmux pane output (which can include `echo $GITHUB_TOKEN`, accidentally pasted credentials, or LLM-replayed secrets from training data) flows into the monitor's emitted JSON without filtering. The same JSON is consumed by orchestration scripts and may end up in logs, dispatch state DBs, or `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/` files.\\n\\nSymptom: a kage-bunshin agent that runs `env | grep TOKEN` (or pastes a curl command with a header) leaks secrets to the monitor output and to any downstream consumer. There is no defense-in-depth at the boundary that captures and redistributes that text.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2690c9f6a9f0856fe42e6772d9ced6d02709b741fa8f0252f98646577189dd50\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPukpGg\"}"}